  "note": "Copy-slack measurements: the file set was created by the program right on the mounted empty volume, and the left space was read after remounting. Only measured values are stored; the slack itself is derived from them. The file counts differ on purpose: a single n gives no slope at all. The two sets with n = 1 differ in size (64 MiB and 4 GiB) and gave the same slack — which is how it was checked that slack depends on the file count, not on the file size. An own measurement of the same set always supersedes the factory one. The empty volume of each was measured before the files were written, so each also gives an NTFS metadata point — on \"non-round\" volumes between the recommended sizes.",
